# Action creators — one per `Action` variant

## Context

`app/src/actions.ts` holds one creator per `Action` variant (`addTask`,
`toggleTask`, `removeTask`, `setFilter`) — the sanctioned way to build
`Action` objects.

## Rule

- Every new `Action` variant added to `app/src/types.ts` gets a matching
  named-export creator function in `app/src/actions.ts`, named
  `verbNoun`/`verb` (e.g. `addTask`, `setFilter`) — not `createAddTask` or
  `taskAddedAction`.
- Match the existing `type` string convention: `"<domain>/<verb in past
  tense>"` (`task/added`, `task/toggled`, `task/removed`, `filter/set`), not
  `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` or a bare verb.
- Action creators only build and return an `Action` object — they never call
  `dispatch` themselves and never contain reducer logic (no branching on
  existing state).
- Consumers/tests dispatch via the creator (`store.dispatch(addTask(...))`),
  not by hand-writing `{ type: "...", payload: {...} }` inline.

## How to verify

1. The number of `type:` variants in the `Action` union
   (`app/src/types.ts`) equals the number of exported creator functions in
   `app/src/actions.ts`.
2. `grep -n "type: \"" app/src/**/*.ts` outside of `types.ts`/`actions.ts`/
   `reducer.ts`/`*.test.ts` returns no matches — nothing builds raw action
   objects by hand elsewhere.
3. New `type` strings match `^[a-z]+\/[a-z]+$` and read as past tense
   (`added`/`removed`/`toggled`/`set`), consistent with the existing four.
4. `cd app && npm test` passes, including a test exercising the new creator.